       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. The usual adult range is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily, and 5 mg is the typical starting dose. A dose of 50 mg risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, those effects can last for days. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify a dose that high.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 5 mg intended. Which of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the standard starting dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n3. **A different dose you specify.**\n4. **50 mg exactly as written**, if it's intentional. Please confirm the dose and the clinical rationale, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
      }
